From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:05:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 071/138] pinctrl: apple: Let GPIO interrupts be wakeup sources

The GPIO irqchip has no irq_set_wake, so enable_irq_wake() fails with
-ENXIO and gpio-keys aborts system suspend on the "wakeup-source"
Home and Power buttons. The pin controller needs no setup to wake the
system from suspend-to-idle (the AIC keeps delivering the bank
interrupt while the CPUs sit in WFI), so mark the chip
IRQCHIP_SKIP_SET_WAKE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-apple-gpio.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-apple-gpio.c b/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-apple-gpio.c
index 6305b96aa..2d132ab51 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-apple-gpio.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-apple-gpio.c
@@ -367,7 +367,7 @@ static const struct irq_chip apple_gpio_irqchip = {
 	.irq_mask		= apple_gpio_irq_mask,
 	.irq_unmask		= apple_gpio_irq_unmask,
 	.irq_set_type		= apple_gpio_irq_set_type,
-	.flags			= IRQCHIP_IMMUTABLE,
+	.flags			= IRQCHIP_IMMUTABLE | IRQCHIP_SKIP_SET_WAKE,
 	GPIOCHIP_IRQ_RESOURCE_HELPERS,
 };
 
